\newlabel{fig:problem_formulation}{{2}{3}{The geometric constraints between a cylinder $\mathcal {C}_j$ and one of its silhouette lines $l^h_{ij}$. The backprojection of $l^h_{ij}$ is a plane $\Pi ^h_{ij}$ tangent to $C_{ij}$ \eqref {eq:dual_quadric_constraint} and passing to the point at infinity of the cylinder\eqref {eq:expanded_vertex_constraint}, \emph {i.e.}, parallel to its axis}{figure.caption.2}{}}
